Significance: patch
Type: fix

Restore two payment token query contracts changed unreleased in #66607: get_tokens() honors an explicit limit of 0 again (returns no rows, so extensions returning 0 from woocommerce_get_customer_payment_tokens_limit hide saved methods), and a page argument passed without a limit paginates again instead of being ignored, so paginating consumers looping until an empty page terminate. Such a page is now sized by a default of 100, filterable via the new woocommerce_get_payment_tokens_page_size, rather than by the site's posts_per_page option as in earlier releases. A woocommerce_get_customer_payment_tokens_limit callback returning a non-numeric value (such as a conditional callback with no else branch) now falls back to the documented default instead of leaving the saved methods query unbounded.
